      "side": 1,
      "message": "This actually works differently than I thought. It\u0027s making a blocking call to each hook in sequence. I was thinking it was just scheduling them for later, but that\u0027s `hook_call_deferred`.\n\nThat means that most of the time taken by this function is probably in the actual hooks, and that would be an interesting thing to measure.\n\nIt may be that we can change the `hook_notify` call to a `hook_call_deferred` call and save some time on the critical path. But that will depend on what the hooks need to do.",
      "revId": "d3341954a26c8f826719f6ebd9fb638f4670545e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
